From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mio <mio@mio19.uk>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:38:31 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] raumata: keep each stack on its share of the radio

The airtime gate now sees the port recorded before encryption, MeshCore transmits no longer wedge when the radio is busy, and a Meshtastic app edit is put back onto the chip in a MeshCore-profile mode.

diff --git a/docs/raumata-dual-protocol.md b/docs/raumata-dual-protocol.md
index f2dc07870d83a9e836bc310a6311de0b6f3f89e9..a617e5326aa153c06ebab85353e8efa17b0257e7 100644
--- a/docs/raumata-dual-protocol.md
+++ b/docs/raumata-dual-protocol.md
@@ -99,11 +99,12 @@ keep the Raumata link record, operating mode, and presence schedule.
 
 ## Companion interface
 
-A USB-serial mux parses both Meshtastic (`0x94 0xC3`) and MeshCore (`<`)
-framing. With `RAUMATA_COMPANION_MODE_BLE_USB=1` (enabled by default in
-`heltec-v3-dual`), USB starts in MeshCore companion mode so a Meshtastic app can
-connect over BLE while a MeshCore app connects over USB simultaneously without
-debug log or `FromRadio` queue contention.
+A USB-serial mux parses both Meshtastic (`0x94 0xC3`, big-endian length) and
+MeshCore (`<`, little-endian length) framing. With
+`RAUMATA_COMPANION_MODE_BLE_USB=1` (enabled by default in `heltec-v3-dual` and
+the T-Deck dual environments), USB ignores Meshtastic framing and stays in
+MeshCore companion mode, so a Meshtastic app can connect over BLE while a
+MeshCore app connects over USB without debug log or `FromRadio` contention.
 
 ## Build
 
